[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2847043172","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105994#issuecomment-2847043172","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105994","id":2847043172,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6psm5k","user":{"login":"llama-nl","id":94882246,"node_id":"U_kgDOBafJxg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/94882246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/llama-nl","html_url":"https://github.com/llama-nl","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/llama-nl/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/llama-nl/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/llama-nl/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/llama-nl/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/llama-nl/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/llama-nl/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/llama-nl/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/llama-nl/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/llama-nl/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-02T12:00:08Z","updated_at":"2025-05-02T12:00:08Z","body":"The spacing feels excessive to me. Also, the side ActionPanel and this change make the editor viewport quite small. It would be much better if the editor could be set to full screen by default on Android. That would greatly improve usability with those changes. ","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2847043172/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2847243663","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105994#issuecomment-2847243663","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105994","id":2847243663,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ptX2P","user":{"login":"m4gr3d","id":914968,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkxNDk2OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/914968?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d","html_url":"https://github.com/m4gr3d","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-02T13:41:58Z","updated_at":"2025-05-02T13:41:58Z","body":"I agree with the spacing feeling excessive. I think we should instead go with the option in the proposal and add a larger drag handle instead of increasing the whole bar.\n\nWhile on the topic of larger drag handle, we should try to do the same for the scrollbars, as in keep the width of the scrollbars the same as on desktop, but increase the width of the scrollbars handle to make it easier to drag.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2847243663/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2847275551","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105994#issuecomment-2847275551","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105994","id":2847275551,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ptfof","user":{"login":"m4gr3d","id":914968,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkxNDk2OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/914968?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d","html_url":"https://github.com/m4gr3d","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-02T13:57:47Z","updated_at":"2025-05-02T13:57:47Z","body":"> I think we should instead go with the option in the proposal and add a larger drag handle instead of increasing the whole bar.\n\nWe should make the drag handle / dragger semi transparent, so it doesn't obscure the content behind it.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2847275551/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2847290294","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105994#issuecomment-2847290294","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105994","id":2847290294,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ptjO2","user":{"login":"syntaxerror247","id":176927541,"node_id":"U_kgDOCouzNQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/176927541?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247","html_url":"https://github.com/syntaxerror247","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-02T14:05:00Z","updated_at":"2025-05-02T14:05:00Z","body":"@llama-nl @m4gr3d I felt the same way when I first tried it, but after using it for a while, I think it's a fair tradeoff -- it improves usability more than it takes up space.\r\n\r\n> I think we should instead go with the option in the proposal and add a larger drag handle instead of increasing the whole bar.\r\n\r\nI don't think that's possible. Enlarging the drag handle also increases the separation, since it still has to fit within that. Dragger can't go beyond the boundaries. \r\nThere's an option to increase the drag area while keeping it visually the same, but that causes issues because items within that area wouldn’t be focusable/usable anymore.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2847290294/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2847327639","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105994#issuecomment-2847327639","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105994","id":2847327639,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ptsWX","user":{"login":"kitbdev","id":10054226,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMDU0MjI2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10054226?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev","html_url":"https://github.com/kitbdev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-02T14:18:50Z","updated_at":"2025-05-02T14:18:50Z","body":"It should actually be possible since https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/72680, the drag handle is exposed and a child can be added to it to act as another handle. But adding a child would have to be done for each one.\r\nOr a setting can be added to SplitContainer to not use the icons size, then the icon would be on top.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2847327639/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2847338616","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105994#issuecomment-2847338616","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105994","id":2847338616,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ptvB4","user":{"login":"m4gr3d","id":914968,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkxNDk2OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/914968?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d","html_url":"https://github.com/m4gr3d","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-02T14:23:59Z","updated_at":"2025-05-02T14:23:59Z","body":"> @llama-nl @m4gr3d I felt the same way when I first tried it, but after using it for a while, I think it's a fair tradeoff -- it improves usability more than it takes up space.\n> \n\nWe are wasting too much space with this approach, the visible handle itself takes only a small section but we are wasting the whole vertical space. The same thing happens for the scrollbars, which I have never been happy with, but given our initial guidance was to use a keyboard+mouse, it was a lower priority item to address.\nHere though, we are prioritizing improving the touch experience so we need to address those issues.\n\n> > I think we should instead go with the option in the proposal and add a larger drag handle instead of increasing the whole bar.\n> \n> I don't think that's possible. Enlarging the drag handle also increases the separation, since it still has to fit within that. Dragger can't go beyond the boundaries. \n\nWell, let's look into addressing that, either we use a different component on Android for the split area drag handle and for the scrollbars drag handle, or we update those components to support the described behaviors.\nIf we are running into those issues, then others will likely run into the same when building their apps / games with Godot. By addressing those issues we are unblocking those use-cases alongside improving the user experience.\n\n> There's an option to increase the drag area while keeping it visually the same, but that causes issues because items within that area wouldn’t be focusable/usable anymore.\n\nIn this case, I'd looking to increase the drag handle area only, so it's easier for users to target it and drag it around. The drag handle as shown in the proposal would still be small enough that it would not affect other items that are adjacent to it.\n\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2847338616/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2847342764","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105994#issuecomment-2847342764","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105994","id":2847342764,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ptwCs","user":{"login":"m4gr3d","id":914968,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkxNDk2OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/914968?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d","html_url":"https://github.com/m4gr3d","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-02T14:25:59Z","updated_at":"2025-05-02T14:25:59Z","body":"> It should actually be possible since https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/72680, the drag handle is exposed and a child can be added to it to act as another handle. But adding a child would have to be done for each one.\n> Or a setting can be added to SplitContainer to not use the icons size, then the icon would be on top.\n\n@kitbdev thanks for the reference, that looks exactly like what I had in mind!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2847342764/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2847357966","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105994#issuecomment-2847357966","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105994","id":2847357966,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ptzwO","user":{"login":"m4gr3d","id":914968,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkxNDk2OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/914968?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d","html_url":"https://github.com/m4gr3d","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-02T14:32:53Z","updated_at":"2025-05-02T14:32:53Z","body":"> > It should actually be possible since https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/72680, the drag handle is exposed and a child can be added to it to act as another handle. But adding a child would have to be done for each one.\n> > Or a setting can be added to SplitContainer to not use the icons size, then the icon would be on top.\n> \n> @kitbdev thanks for the reference, that looks exactly like what I had in mind!\n\n@syntaxerror247 based on the feature in the referenced PR, I'm thinking at a high level, the approach could consist of adding a larger button to the drag handle for both the split container and the scrollbars. Dragging the added button (vertically for the scrollbars, horizontally for the split container) would accordingly scroll the scrollbars up/down, resize the split container.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2847357966/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2847361280","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105994#issuecomment-2847361280","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105994","id":2847361280,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6pt0kA","user":{"login":"syntaxerror247","id":176927541,"node_id":"U_kgDOCouzNQ","avatar_url":"https://